``` Detection: Windows password spray / brute force (T1110)
    Data: Windows Security event logs (EventCode 4625 = failed logon).
    Logic: one source hitting many distinct accounts in a short window. ```

index=wineventlog sourcetype=WinEventLog:Security EventCode=4625
| bucket _time span=10m
| stats count as failures
        dc(Account_Name) as distinct_accounts
        values(Account_Name) as targeted_accounts
        by src_ip, _time
| where failures > 20 AND distinct_accounts >= 5
| sort - failures

``` Follow-up: correlate with a subsequent EventCode 4624 (success) from the same
    src_ip to confirm spray-to-compromise, then trigger the compromised-account playbook.
    Tuning: allow-list service accounts / scanners; adjust thresholds per environment size. ```
